course: dictionary
lesson: 11694
title: Attended: went to, or looked after
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Attended is a verb, and its past form is attended. It means went to an event, a meeting or a place, like a school, a party or a game. «Over two hundred fans attended the match on Saturday.» The fans went to the match, so attended means were there.
explain: Attended can also mean looked after or dealt with someone or something. «The nurse attended to the boy's cut.» The nurse did not go anywhere here. She took care of the cut, so attended to means looked after.
explain: The words around attended tell you which meaning it has. Ask: did someone go to a place, or did someone take care of a person or a problem? Then swap in went to or looked after and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Attended means went to an event, a meeting or a place.
fact: Attended to means looked after or dealt with.
fact: Attendance is the number of people who were at an event, such as «The attendance at the concert was high.»
fact: You can say «attended school» to mean went to school regularly, as in «She attended the same school for six years.»
fact: Numbers of people at events can be counted, added and compared: 40 attended on Monday and 55 attended on Tuesday, so Tuesday had more.
exercise: «Over two hundred fans attended the match on Saturday.» What does attended mean here? | Wrote about | Ran away from | Forgot | *Went to
exercise: «The nurse attended to the boy's cut.» What does attended to mean here? | Painted | Went to the moon | Ignored | *Looked after
exercise: Which word is the past form of attend? | *attended | attend | attends | attending
test: «Only twelve people attended the meeting, so the room felt empty.» What does attended mean here? | Sang at | Were not at | *Were present at | Sat on
test: «Dad attended to the dog after it hurt its paw.» What does attended to mean here? | *Took care of | Ran away from | Went to the shops
exam: «The school had good attendance, with almost every pupil attending every day.» What does attendance mean? | *The number of pupils who came | The lunch menu | A type of school bag
